Z||000000||Ronnie||01-15-2001||07:57 PM||||Can somebody tell me how you identify the 4 spd with 4:10 gears. Are all 84 model 4 spds. the 4:10 gear.If they are, I might have spotted one today at the salvage yard!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero2_1_3.jpg">  '86 GT 4-speed, leather interior||||reg||6
Z||000001||mrfiero||01-15-2001||08:06 PM||||Not all '84 4-speeds are 4.10, but most are.  There were about 5000 or so 3.32 4-speeds in '84.  The only real way to tell them apart is by looking at the option sticker on the inside wheel well (under hood).  The 4.10 tranny has the code M19 and the 3.32 tranny has the code MY8.<P>If the '84 is an SE then it will have the 4.10.<P>I hope this helps.<BR>   ||||reg||1
